-- title:
--   Theorem B.3 — position sum satisfies uniform pumping but is not CCRA-computable
-- statement:
--   On a bit word $b_1\cdots b_j$, let
--
--   $$
--   f(b_1\cdots b_j)=\sum_{i=1}^j i b_i.
--   $$
--
--   This position-sum function satisfies the complete uniform pumping condition over the finitely generated subsemiring $R=\mathbb Z[1/2]$ with the uniform exponent $m=1$: for every words $u,w,v$, the sequence
--
--   $$
--   \big(f(uw^{n+1}v)\big)_{n\ge0}
--   $$
--
--   is $R$-generable and every degree coefficient sum $S_j$ of its exponential-polynomial representation belongs to $R$. Nevertheless, no CCRA over $\mathbb Q$ computes $f$.
--
--   This separates the necessary uniform pumping condition from CCRA recognizability.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: bits, $\mathbb Z[1/2]$, generable sequences and exponential-polynomial coefficient sums are given operational Lean definitions → `Bool` encodes $0/1$, the subsemiring is generated by $-1$ and $1/2$, and finite sums/products and distinct nonzero bases are explicit; reason: these choices implement exactly the definitions restated on pp.15–16 without changing an instance
-- source:
--   Zeng–Cao–Dai–Wang–Ding, Copyless Cost Register Automata and Algebraic Groups, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 434d3094df2665371c402d5b5291b3c7f3a27a0d79384e4a8ec3ca3a46a92543), Theorem B.3, p.15 (PDF p.17); proof p.16 (PDF p.18)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CopylessCRA_Supplement_UniformPumping

namespace CopylessCRA
namespace Supplement

/-- Zeng--Cao--Dai--Wang--Ding, *Copyless Cost Register Automata and Algebraic Groups*, STOC
2027 submission (manuscript sha256 434d3094...), Theorem B.3, p.15 (PDF p.17), proof p.16
(PDF p.18).  The position sum satisfies the complete uniform pumping condition over the finitely
generated subsemiring `ℤ[1/2]` with the one exponent `m = 1`, independent of all context words,
but no CCRA over `ℚ` computes it.

**Formalization Note** Boolean `false/true` encode the bits `0/1`, positions start at one, and
`UniformPumping` includes both `R`-generability and every exponential-polynomial coefficient-sum
condition. -/
theorem theorem_B_3 : UniformPumping dyadicSemiring 1 positionSum ∧ ¬ C1 positionSum := by sorry

end Supplement
end CopylessCRA
